  "aiOverview": {
    "content": "Hanwha Group is a major South Korean Fortune Global 500 chaebol founded in 1952, with 2024 total sales of $64.1B. It is a global leader in aerospace, defense, energy (solar/hydrogen), finance, and shipbuilding, focused on sustainable solutions and advanced technology. Key Industries and Operations Aerospace & Defense: Hanwha Aerospace is a leading producer of aircraft engines (10,000+ produced), defense systems (K9 Thunder, Redback IFV), and space technology. Energy & Ocean Solutions: Hanwha Solutions (Qcells) is a dominant solar energy provider. Hanwha Ocean (formerly DSME) produces high-end vessels, and Hanwha Philly Shipyard operates in the U.S.. Finance & Services: Offers, insurance, securities, and asset management. Machinery & Vision: Produces industrial equipment and high-tech AI surveillance solutions (Hanwha Vision). Key Milestones and History 1952: Founded as Korea Explosives Co.. 1992: Adopted the name \"Hanwha\". 2000s-Present: Expanded into solar energy (acquiring Qcells), aerospace, and shipbuilding (acquiring DSME in 2023). 2024: Named to the TIME100 Most Influential Companies list. LeadershipHanwha is ranked among the top 7 business groups in South Korea as of 2024. Jae-il Son is the President & CEO of Hanwha Aerospace. Key Products and Services Defense: Self-propelled guns, armored vehicles, precision-guided weapons. Solar: Solar cells, modules, and energy systems. Aerospace: Aircraft engines, satellite systems. Shipbuilding: LNG carriers, warships. Security: Surveillance cameras and AI-powered video analytics.",
